  "name": "Question 18",
  "problem": "Find the disjoint union of the sets ${A}_{1}={3,a,7}$ and ${A}_{2}={a,b}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Notice that the sets are overlapping since\n\n$$\n{3,a,7}\\cap {a,b}={a}\\ne \u2205.\n$$\n\nSo, for each of our sets, we form the associated set, where each element is tagged with the corresponding index, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {A}_{1} &  & \\,\\to \\, &  & {A}_{1}^{\u2217}={(3,1),(a,1),(7,1)} \\\\  & {A}_{2} &  & \\,\\to \\, &  & {A}_{2}^{\u2217}={(a,2),(b,2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the disjoint union of our sets is simply the union of the associated tagged sets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}\u2294{A}_{2} & ={3,a,7}\u2294{a,b} \\\\  & ={A}_{1}^{\u2217}\\cup {A}_{2}^{\u2217} \\\\  & ={(3,1),(a,1),(7,1)}\\cup {(a,2),(b,2)} \\\\  & ={(3,1),(a,1),(7,1),(a,2),(b,2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
